analysisWe need to assess each element. Scope: yes, there was an assembly (flash mob). He tried to participate. It was peaceful. So scope yes.

Interference: Police dispersed, charged, fined. Yes interference.

Prescribed by law: The law requires notification; they didn't notify. But is the law foreseeably applied? The law applies to static demonstrations with multiple persons. This was such. So yes prescribed. Also accessible? The law is published. Safeguards? There's possibility of discretion but likely adequate. So yes.

Legitimate aim: The aim could be public safety/prevention of disorder. Police dispersal due to lack of notification maybe aimed at preventing disorder. So yes.

Necessity: Need to weigh. The protest was peaceful, no threat. Dispersal and fine may be disproportionate. Likely necessity fails. So no.

Positive obligation: None.

